			"date": "2024-08-09T15:50:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Ah, cool!  A lot of it depends on where you’ll be. I’m most familiar with the south, the region where I live. I usually recommend Þjórsárdalur valley <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Þjórsárdalur\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Þjórsárd</span><span class=\"invisible\">alur</span></a> (was there literally last week 🙂)</p><p>More to the east you have Kirkjubæjarklaustur, a historically notable village in an interesting area <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkjubæjarklaustur\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkjubæ</span><span class=\"invisible\">jarklaustur</span></a></p><p>And a little bit beyond that you have Skaftafell national park full of amazing landmarks <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skaftafell\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skaftafe</span><span class=\"invisible\">ll</span></a></p><p>That’s off the top of my head 🙂</p>",
